        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Curse Ye Scallywags!"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(curse, divine, necromancy)\n\nWhen the ghost pirate captain is reduced to 0 HP, all creatures within 60 feet are subjected to a 25 mariner's curse spell. The locations of those that critically fail are known to the ghost until the curse is removed. This curse ends if the ghost is permanently destroyed."
            },
            "id": "e055dda0-8ffa-4ff3-8e04-24a58b520f5c",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-04-15T14:13:02.505956"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Rejuvenation"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(divine, necromancy)\n\nWhen the ghost pirate captain is destroyed, they re-form after 2d4 days within the ship or location they're bound to, fully healed. They can be permanently destroyed if their desires are fulfilled, which could involve being defeated in a great battle or ensuring their treasure has been hidden."
            },
            "id": "578dd4d3-4f19-4797-a859-7a17012bd4aa",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-04-15T14:13:02.505956"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Ship Bound"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "The ghost is typically bound to a vessel, even one damaged beyond repair. They can't venture more than 120 feet away from the ship or site of its wreckage."
            },
